      "writtenOn": "2017-02-28T18:03:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would strongly encourage you to document the specific purposes of each part of the global_buf - that is, which part (where and how much) is being used as the AES key, and which part (where and how much) is being used as the nonce.  The current code conflates these two uses (and perhaps others if there are any??) into a single flat array, with magic incantations like \"p+16\".\n\nI\u0027d be happier if you turned global_buf into a C union - one aspect being the array of  samples that you\u0027re filling it with, and another being a clear structure definition of the AES key and nonce.  I think the runtime code would be nearly or completely identical, and it would be much easier for a reader to understand and analyze.",
      "revId": "390d1433698abcbe3363e6a59c5c2d4d0b7ef0db",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
